  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "State Of Gujarat - Thro' J A Shah vs Dipak Ramchandra Majmudar on 22 January, 2016",
    "facts": "By way of this application, the State has challenged the order dated 12.4.2010 passed by the learned Chief Judicial Magistrate, Bhavnagar passed below application Exh.16 in Criminal Case No.4336 of 2009 by which learned Magistrate has discharged the respondent-accused while exercising the powers under Section 245(2) of Criminal Procedure Code, 1973. Learned APP submitted that on 15.5.2009, Food Inspector visited the shop of the respondent-accused along with panchas. The respondent-accused was carrying on the business in the name and style of Gujarat Juice situated at Bhavnagar. Accused was present there. The Food Inspector, after following procedure prescribed under the Prevention of Food Adulteration and rules framed thereunder, took the samples, one sample was forwarded to the public analyst, Rajkot and two bags of the samples were sent to the Local Health Authority for analysis who has given the opinion in his report dated 18.6.2009 that the samples of Mango Milk Shake is adulterated and the same is in contravention of Rule 29 of the Prevention of The Prevention of Food Adulteration Rules, 1955. The Food Inspector thereafter obtained the consent from the competent authority for filing the HC-NIC Page 2 of 5 Created On Tue Jan 26 02:23:59 IST 2016 R/CR.RA/446/2011 JUDGMENT complaint against the respondent-accused. Accordingly, the complaint being Criminal Case No.4336 of 2009 came to be filed. At this stage, learned APP submitted that the respondent-accused filed an application Exh.16 under Section 245(2) of the Code for discharging him from the aforesaid case. Learned Chief Judicial Magistrate, Bhavnagar by the impugned order discharged the accused. The applicant-State has therefore preferred this application.",
    "arguments": "3. Learned APP mainly contended that the trial Court has wrongly discharged the respondent-accused from the charges levelled against him only relying upon the report given by the Central Food Laboratory.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. Learned APP mainly contended that the trial Court has wrongly discharged the respondent-accused from the charges levelled against him only relying upon the report given by the Central Food Laboratory.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
